University Research Institutes Research Facilities About Our History Facts and Figures University Vision and Mission Welcoming to All Accessibility Alumni Network Leadership and Administration Partnerships and Community Relations Living in Central New York Help and Contacts Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Search Helpful Links Academic Calendars Events Human Resources MySlice Registrar Libraries Syracuse University Academics Career Paths Social Sciences Career Path Use your insights into human behavior and institutions in a career that enhances individual lives and our broader social systems. Social Sciences Architecture Art and Design Business and Finance Communications and Writing Education Engineering Health and Human Services Humanities and Languages Law and Government Performing Arts Science and Mathematics Social Justice and Advocacy Social Sciences Sports Technology, Data and AI Career Options With a degree in social sciences, you’ll open doors in fields ranging from psychology to international relations to urban planning and beyond. Archaeologist Field Technician Cybersecurity Analyst Diplomat Environmental Specialist FEMA Corps Member Global Operations Analyst Labor Relations Specialist Legislative Aide Lobbyist Policy Analyst Stats and Facts # 1 Best Public Affairs Schools (U.S. News & World Report) # 9 International Global Policy and Administration (U.S. News & World Report) # 6 Social Policy (U.S. News & World Report) 110 + Study Abroad Programs Learn more about study abroad Discover Social Sciences Majors and Minors Pursue your interests with a customizable social sciences program that sets you up for success. Explore programs Coursework Highlights Find courses that give you the knowledge and skills to stand out from the pack. AI and Environmental Policy Cognitive Psychology Environmental Ethics Ethnographic Techniques Firearms and Impression Evidence Forensic Chemical Analysis Global Community Peace, War and Security Psychology of Childhood Research in Civic Engagement Featured Employers Our graduates land jobs with top employers. Accenture Embassy of Spain in the U.S. - Education Office KPMG New York State Senate Peace Corps Pfizer SUNY Upstate Medical University U.S. Department of Labor U.S. House of Representatives Teach for America Learn more about degree outcomes As an aspiring physician, I have to understand the social determinants of health that guide medical care. Being in the city of Syracuse gave me the perspective on the joys, struggles and hopes of the people that I will serve. Louis Smith '23 Citizenship and Civic Engagement B.A. and Biology B.S. , Maxwell School of Citizenship and Public Affairs and College of Arts and Sciences Clubs and Organizations Learning happens inside and outside the classroom. Make connections to build your resume and your network. Best Buddies International at SU Economics Student Association Model United Nations Club New York Public Interest Research Group Psychology Club Public Administration and International Relations Association Request More Information Loading... Start your application Start your academic journey with us. Apply Explore affordability Learn about grants and scholarships. Learn more Schedule a tour Plan your visit and get ready to make yourself at home. Visit us 900 South Crouse Ave. Syracuse, NY 13244 315.443.1870 Contact Us Emergency Contact Academics Admissions and Aid Campus Life Research About Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Blackboard MySlice Stories Campus Map Campus Store Work at Syracuse Human Resources Syracuse University Brand Accreditation Title IX Accessibility Privacy Policy Consumer Information"
    },
    "http://www.syracuse.edu/academics/career-paths/sports/": {
      "title": "SportsCareer Path",
      "description": "Career Path: Sports - Syracuse University By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies in accordance with our privacy policy . Dismiss Skip to Content Academics Undergraduate Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Online Programs Certificates and Credentials Career Paths Selecting A Major Study Abroad or Away Syracuse University Global Other Academic Opportunities Schools and Colleges Academic Calendars Course Catalog Admissions and Aid Why Syracuse University Start Your Application Application Process Cost of Attendance Financial Aid and Scholarships Tour Campus Request Information Campus Life Living On Campus Living Off Campus Campus Highlights Sports and Recreation Clubs and Organizations Health and Wellness Belonging and Access Veteran and Military Student Services Student Centers Arts at Syracuse University Libraries Research Distinctive Research Excellence Undergraduate Research Graduate Research University Research Institutes Research Facilities About Our History Facts and Figures University Vision and Mission Welcoming to All Accessibility Alumni Network Leadership and Administration Partnerships and Community Relations Living in Central New York Help and Contacts Academics Undergraduate Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Online Programs Certificates and Credentials Career Paths Selecting A Major Study Abroad or Away Syracuse University Global Other Academic Opportunities Schools and Colleges Academic Calendars Course Catalog Admissions and Aid Why Syracuse University Start Your Application Application Process Cost of Attendance Financial Aid and Scholarships Tour Campus Request Information Campus Life Living On Campus Living Off Campus Campus Highlights Sports and Recreation Clubs and Organizations Health and Wellness Belonging and Access Veteran and Military Student Services Student Centers Arts at Syracuse University Libraries Research Distinctive Research Excellence Undergraduate Research Graduate Research University Research Institutes Research Facilities About Our History Facts and Figures University Vision and Mission Welcoming to All Accessibility Alumni Network Leadership and Administration Partnerships and Community Relations Living in Central New York Help and Contacts Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Search Helpful Links Academic Calendars Events Human Resources MySlice Registrar Libraries Syracuse University Academics Career Paths Sports Career Path Break ground, make an impact, and explore your passions in one of today's fastest-growing, in-demand industries. Sports Architecture Art and Design Business and Finance Communications and Writing Education Engineering Health and Human Services Humanities and Languages Law and Government Performing Arts Science and Mathematics Social Justice and Advocacy Social Sciences Sports Technology, Data and AI Career Options With a sports-related degree, you'll be open to opportunities on and off the field. Sports Agent Athletic Coach Sports Broadcaster Sports Photojournalist Event Coordinator Sports Marketing Specialist Sports Finance Executive Sports Data Analyst Facility Operations Manager Fitness Coach Athletic Trainer Stats and Facts 1st Undergraduate Sports Analytics Degree in the United States. # 2 Best Photojournalism Schools (College Factual) # 6 Best Broadcast Journalism Schools (College Factual) # 9 Best Colleges for Sport Management (Niche) Discover Sports Majors and Minors Create a sports-related path that fits your goals and inspires your dreams. Explore programs Coursework Highlights Find courses that fit who you want to be in your profession. Health Sciences Applied to Coaching Nutrition for Fitness and Sports Olympic Odyssey Psycho-Social Issues of Sport Sport Data Analysis Sport Economics Sport Marketing Management Television Sports Anchoring and Reporting The Business of Esports The Philosophy, Principles and Organization of Athletics in Education The Super Bowl: Sport, Culture and Entertainment Featured Employers Our graduates succeed after leaving Syracuse University. Boston Celtics Brooklyn Football Club Buffalo Bills Clemson University Crunch Fitness DraftKings ESPN Fox Sports Green Bay Packers Kraft Sports + Entertainment Los Angeles Lakers Madison Square Garden Minnesota Twins MKTG MLB NBA New York Islanders New York Yankees San Jose Sharks VaynerSports Learn more about degree outcomes One of my biggest takeaways was how many different career paths exist within sports and entertainment venues. Seeing these environments firsthand made the industry feel much more ‘real’ and reinforced my interest in working within sports. Kaden Halboth ’28 Sport Management , David B. Falk College of Sport See his experience See his experience Clubs and Organizations Learning happens inside and outside the classroom. Make connections to build your resume and your network. Baseball Sabermetrics and Statistics Club Basketball Analytics Club Exercise Science Club Gaming Club Mu Sigma Lambda Orange Wrap Pre-Therapy and Allied Health Club Sport & Community Sport Management Club Sportsbook Analytics Club The Nutrition Education and Promotion Association (NEPA) Women in Sports and Events (WISE) Esports At Syracuse University, you can become part of an esports community that will help you develop your skills and power your passion. You'll enjoy our state-of-the-art gaming room. Whether you're a highly competitive gamer or just giving esports a try, you'll find plenty of action and challenges. Learn more about esports Request More Information Loading... Start your application Start your academic journey with us. Apply Explore affordability Learn about grants and scholarships. Learn more Schedule a tour Plan your visit and get ready to make yourself at home. Visit us 900 South Crouse Ave. Syracuse, NY 13244 315.443.1870 Contact Us Emergency Contact Academics Admissions and Aid Campus Life Research About Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Blackboard MySlice Stories Campus Map Campus Store Work at Syracuse Human Resources Syracuse University Brand Accreditation Title IX Accessibility Privacy Policy Consumer Information"
    },
