esearch University Research Institutes Research Facilities About Our History Facts and Figures University Vision and Mission Welcoming to All Accessibility Alumni Network Leadership and Administration Partnerships and Community Relations Living in Central New York Help and Contacts Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Search Helpful Links Academic Calendars Events Human Resources MySlice Registrar Libraries Syracuse University Academics Career Paths Technology, Data and AI Career Path Drive decision-making and lead change managing the systems and tools that are shaping the future of every industry. Technology, Data and AI Architecture Art and Design Business and Finance Communications and Writing Education Engineering Health and Human Services Humanities and Languages Law and Government Performing Arts Science and Mathematics Social Justice and Advocacy Social Sciences Sports Technology, Data and AI Career Options With a degree in technology, data and AI, you’ll open doors in fields ranging from finance to sports, health care to government and beyond. AI Architect AI Ethicist / Compliance Officer Cybersecurity Analyst Data Scientist Digital Marketing Manager LLM Specialist Network Administrator Social Media Manager Software Engineer Sport Data Analyst User Experience Designer Web Developer Stats and Facts # 6 in Best Library and Information Studies Programs (U.S. News & World Report) # 16 Best Information Science Bachelor's Degree Schools (College Factual) 1st Undergraduate Sports Analytics Degree in the United States. 13 + AI-Related Academic Programs. Discover Technology, Data and AI Majors and Minors Pursue your interests with a customizable technology, data or AI program that sets you up for success. Explore programs Coursework Highlights Find courses that give you the knowledge and skills to stand out from the pack. AI Science Ethics and Governance Design of Operating Systems Elements of Computer Science Human-Centered Design Minds and Machines Mobile Forensics and Social Networking Security in a Networked Environment Sport Data Analysis Statistical Methods for Data Science Technical Fundamentals of Artificial Intelligence Technology and the Future of Work Featured Employers Our graduates land jobs with top employers. Apple Amazon Deloitte DraftKings Epic EY IBM JPMorgan Chase Micron Microsoft Morgan Stanley T-Mobile USA, Inc. Learn more about degree outcomes Through our projects, we’ve been able to get a better understanding of the good and bad side of AI, not only have we developed our technical understanding of things but also our ability to think more ethically and see how this can impact people. Daniel Canhedo ’27 Computer Science B.S. , School of Information Studies Learn about his work Learn about his work Clubs and Organizations Learning happens inside and outside the classroom. Make connections to build your resume and your network. American Institute of Aeronautics and Astronautics Information Security Club Innovate Orange Kappa Theta Pi New Explorations in Information Science (NEXIS) Technology Lab Q-SPARK Worldwide Innovation Technology (WiTech) Biotechnology Society at Syracuse University Request More Information Loading... Start your application Start your academic journey with us. Apply Explore affordability Learn about grants and scholarships. Learn more Schedule a tour Plan your visit and get ready to make yourself at home. Visit us 900 South Crouse Ave. Syracuse, NY 13244 315.443.1870 Contact Us Emergency Contact Academics Admissions and Aid Campus Life Research About Athletics Alumni Network News Events Make a Gift Information for Admitted Students Current Students Veteran and Military Students Faculty and Staff Alumni Community and Visitors Parents and Families Blackboard MySlice Stories Campus Map Campus Store Work at Syracuse Human Resources